  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Education for Early Learners (PEEL)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  This activity produces and broadcasts audio visual episodes for television to support the education of early learners.  In addition to the television program, an innovative teacher training program that gives teachers the tools and knowledge they need to create a supportive and interactive classroom environment, incorporating inclusive education strategies.  Other school-based interventions will engage children at pre-primary and early primary levels with educational content that addresses issues of Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion (DEI.) Community-level interventions. This early learners&apos; activity supports two USAID Education Policy priorities: 1) increasing access to quality education for pre-primary aged children, particularly the most marginalized and vulnerable, and 2) preparing children for school by developing their literacy, numeracy, and social-emotional skills. With FY 2022 funds, USAID will improve the learning outcomes of marginalized, pre-primary and primary level children in private/non-government organization schools. The activity will support the education of early learners through the development and broadcasting of television programs; development and distribution of video episodes and other education materials to schools; training of teachers; and increasing awareness of communities, parents, caregivers, and teachers to ensure their support towards ensuring quality education of marginalized children. This activity will meet the basic education ($650,000) earmark.</narrative>
  </description>
